{"page":"TGFBR1","gene":"TGFBR1","accession":"P36897","protein":"TGF-beta receptor type-1","length":503,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"P36897-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000374994.9"],"refseq":["NM_004612.4"],"refseqProteins":["NP_004603.1"],"maneSelect":true,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-P36897-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P36897-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":84.2,"plddt":[[0,31],[50,1],[70,1],[90,5],[70,7],[90,13],[70,10],[90,5],[70,24],[90,11],[70,3],[50,3],[0,7],[50,5],[70,9],[90,9],[70,7],[50,3],[0,19],[50,2],[70,6],[50,16],[70,1],[50,1],[70,4],[90,8],[70,6],[90,7],[70,2],[90,41],[70,5],[90,50],[70,2],[90,42],[70,7],[90,125],[70,4],[50,1]]}},"features":[{"type":"Signal","start":1,"end":33,"description":""},{"type":"Topological domain","start":34,"end":126,"description":"Extracellular"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":36,"end":54,"description":""},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":38,"end":41,"description":""},{"type":"Glycosylation","start":45,"end":45,"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine"},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":48,"end":71,"description":""},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":86,"end":100,"description":""},{"type":"Disulfide bond","start":101,"end":106,"description":""},{"type":"Transmembrane","start":127,"end":147,"description":"Helical"},{"type":"Topological domain","start":148,"end":503,"description":"Cytoplasmic"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":165,"end":165,"description":"Phosphoserine"},{"type":"Domain","start":175,"end":204,"description":"GS"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":185,"end":185,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by TGFBR2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":186,"end":186,"description":"Phosphothreonine; by TGFBR2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":187,"end":187,"description":"Phosphoserine; by TGFBR2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":189,"end":189,"description":"Phosphoserine; by TGFBR2"},{"type":"Modified residue","start":191,"end":191,"description":"Phosphoserine; by TGFBR2"},{"type":"Motif","start":193,"end":194,"description":"FKBP1A-binding"},{"type":"Domain","start":205,"end":495,"description":"Protein kinase"},{"type":"Binding site","start":211,"end":219,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Binding site","start":232,"end":232,"description":"ATP"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":268,"end":268,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in ubiquitin)"},{"type":"Active site","start":333,"end":333,"description":"Proton acceptor"},{"type":"Cross-link","start":391,"end":391,"description":"Glycyl lysine isopeptide (Lys-Gly) (interchain with G-Cter in SUMO)"}],"interfaces":{},"subunit":[{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Homodimer; in the endoplasmic reticulum but also at the cell membrane. Heterohexamer; TGFB1, TGFB2 and TGFB3 homodimeric ligands assemble a functional receptor composed of two TGFBR1 and TGFBR2 heterodimers to form a ligand-receptor heterohexamer. The respective affinity of TGBRB1 and TGFBR2 for the ligands may modulate the kinetics of assembly of the receptor and may explain the different biological activities of TGFB1, TGFB2 and TGFB3. Component of a complex composed of TSC22D1 (via N-terminus), TGFBR1 and TGFBR2; the interaction between TSC22D1 and TGFBR1 is inhibited by SMAD7 and promoted by TGFB1 (PubMed:21791611). Interacts with CD109; inhibits TGF-beta receptor activation in keratinocytes. Interacts with RBPMS. Interacts (unphosphorylated) with FKBP1A; prevents TGFBR1 phosphorylation by TGFBR2 and stabilizes it in the inactive conformation. Interacts with SMAD2, SMAD3 and ZFYVE9; ZFYVE9 recruits SMAD2 and SMAD3 to the TGF-beta receptor. Interacts with TRAF6 and MAP3K7; induces MAP3K7 activation by TRAF6. Interacts with PARD6A; involved in TGF-beta induced epithelial to mesenchymal transition. Interacts with NEDD4L (PubMed:15496141). Interacts with SMAD7, SMURF1 and SMURF2; SMAD7 recruits NEDD4L, SMURF1 and SMURF2 to the TGF-beta receptor (PubMed:11163210, PubMed:11278251). Interacts with USP15 and VPS39. Interacts with SDCBP (via C-terminus) (PubMed:25893292). Interacts with CAV1 and this interaction is impaired in the presence of SDCBP (PubMed:25893292). Interacts with APPL1; interaction is TGF beta dependent; mediates trafficking of the TGFBR1 from the endosomes to the nucleus via microtubules in a TRAF6-dependent manner (PubMed:26583432). Interacts with GPR50; this interaction promotes the constitutive activation of SMAD signaling pathway (PubMed:29572483)"}],"isoforms":[{"accession":"P36897-2","name":"2","synonyms":["B"],"notes":[],"length":507,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000552516.5"],"refseq":["NM_001306210.2"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001293139.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,114],[119,115,389]],"edits":[{"start":114,"end":114,"original":"T","replacement":"TGPFS","added":5}],"missing":0,"replaced":0,"novel":4,"foldedAbsent":0,"foldedMissing":0,"features":[],"interfaces":{},"model":{"entry":"AF-P36897-2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-P36897-2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":84,"plddt":[[0,30],[50,2],[70,1],[90,5],[70,7],[90,13],[70,9],[90,7],[70,23],[90,11],[70,4],[50,3],[0,9],[50,2],[70,2],[50,1],[70,11],[90,8],[70,7],[50,4],[0,15],[50,29],[70,4],[90,8],[70,6],[90,7],[70,2],[90,41],[70,5],[90,49],[70,4],[90,41],[70,2],[50,1],[70,4],[90,125],[70,4],[50,1]],"losingConfidence":0}},{"accession":"P36897-3","name":"3","synonyms":[],"notes":[],"length":426,"transcripts":{"ensembl":["ENST00000374990.6"],"refseq":["NM_001130916.3"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001124388.1"],"maneSelect":false,"decay":[],"onlyDecay":false},"segments":[[1,1,114],[115,192,312]],"edits":[{"start":115,"end":191,"original":"VKSSPGLGPVELAAVIAGPVCFVCISLMLMVYICHNRTVI","replacement":"","added":0}],"missing":77,"replaced":0,"novel":0,"foldedAbsent":31,"foldedMissing":31,"features":[[1,12,0],[8,21,0],[9,44,0],[10,1,0],[11,17,0],[12,1,0],[13,1,0],[14,1,0],[15,1,0],[16,1,0]],"in